  "limits": [
    "Native HTTP send/body await control and observed byte budgets only; no new independently installable subsystem, catalog/auth component or completed harness extraction.",
    "The 1 MiB metadata/64 MiB archive/8 KiB diagnostic limits are intentional compatibility choices, not measured upstream maxima. Counters cover HTTP-wrapper-observed bytes, not unframed wire bytes, headers, expanded ZIP output or total process memory.",
    "Cancellation and 30s per-request send+body deadline are cooperative. Client construction, DNS, underlying blocking work and ordinary Runtime teardown may keep the registered native worker pending beyond the deadline.",
    "No detached drain, bounded native join or complete host-shutdown receipt is introduced. Quarantine remains irreversible; restart alone is not safe recovery.",
    "Original ZIP extractor is unchanged. C2b extraction budgets remain pending rebase and are not included.",
    "Queued callback/config ownership, actual process-final integration and recoverable publication journaling remain open. Existing activation+SHA admitted-region behavior is preserved.",
    "No fresh full CLI/installed-package/GUI/in-app Browser/live-provider or cross-platform runtime acceptance. Earlier full-host descendant failures are not cleared; main is not promoted.",
    "Detailed reports and archives are cloud-local recovery checkpoints, not proven external backups. Source publication is recorded separately.",
    "Upstream provenance mapping is maintained; installed maintenance updater, isolated upstream integration/rollback and polling remain unimplemented."
  ],
